# Force LF line endings across the repo so a Windows checkout (clone /
# pull with core.autocrlf=true, or editors that write CRLF) can't
# reintroduce CR bytes into source files. Rust raw strings `r"..."`
# reject bare CRs at parse time, so this policy keeps the build green
# no matter what OS the developer is on.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# All Rust source must be LF.
*.rs            text eol=lf

# Config + manifest files are also LF (every TOML/JSON viewer we use
# handles LF; CRLF in a Cargo.toml is tolerated but messy in diffs).
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf

# Markdown (README, plan files) — LF so GitHub renders cleanly.
*.md            text eol=lf

# GLSL shader sources — must be LF for the same Rust raw-string reason
# when a `.vert`/`.frag` is included via `include_str!`.
*.glsl          text eol=lf
*.vert          text eol=lf
*.frag          text eol=lf

# Compiled SPIR-V is binary, never normalized.
*.spv           -text
